# Clean Architecture & ASP.NET

Stack: .NET 9, ASP.NET Core Web API, Blazor WASM, EF Core + SQL Server, Identity + JWT, CQRS (MediatR), FluentValidation, AutoMapper, permission policies.

## Layer rules

| Project | May depend on | Owns |
|---------|---------------|------|
| Domain | nothing | entities, enums, `BaseEntity`, `ISoftDelete` |
| Contracts | nothing (or Domain types only if already true) | DTOs/requests shared by API and client |
| Application | Domain, Contracts | commands/queries/handlers, validators, auth policies, repository **interfaces** |
| Infrastructure | Application, Domain | EF, Identity, JWT, repositories, AutoMapper profiles, seeding |
| WebApi | Application, Infrastructure, Contracts | thin controllers, HTTP, Swagger, CORS |
| WebClient | Contracts (via HTTP) | Blazor UI, auth state — never Domain or Infrastructure |

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — business logic in the controller
[HttpPost] public async Task<IActionResult> Create(Case c) { _db.Cases.Add(c); await _db.SaveChangesAsync(); }

// ✅ GOOD — dispatch only
[HttpPost] public async Task<ActionResult<Guid>> Create(CreateCaseCommand command)
    => Ok(await _mediator.Send(command));
```

## Patterns already in use — extend them, do not replace

- CQRS + MediatR; FluentValidation + pipeline behavior
- One repository per aggregate + `IUnitOfWork`; soft delete via `ISoftDelete`
- `[HasPermission(Permissions.X.Y)]` on API actions; thin controllers
- Feature folders under Application (`Cases/Commands`, `Cases/Queries`)

## Clean Code

Small focused types, explicit names, no commented-out code, nullable enabled, prefer constructor injection. Do not introduce a new pattern (e.g. Result, vertical slices, MassTransit) without the architecture-gate question.
